          "rationale": "Test one Mother-authored arithmetic rewrite on the only valid measured base. It cancels the target-mass factor from acceleration and uses rsqrtf; this is a hypothesis, not a confirmed speedup. Keep launch.json unchanged. Complete files:\nsrc/nbody_kernel.cu:\nstruct Particle { float x,y,z,vx,vy,vz,mass; };\nextern \"C\" __global__ void nbody_step_naive(const Particle* in, Particle* out, int n, float dt) {\n  int i=blockIdx.x*blockDim.x+threadIdx.x;\n  if(i>=n) return;\n  const Particle pi=in[i];\n  float ax=0.0f, ay=0.0f, az=0.0f;\n  for(int j=0;j<n;++j) {\n    if(i==j) continue;\n    const Particle pj=in[j];\n    float dx=pj.x-pi.x, dy=pj.y-pi.y, dz=pj.z-pi.z;\n    float r2=dx*dx+dy*dy+dz*dz+0.001f;\n    float invr=rsqrtf(r2);\n    float s=pj.mass*invr*invr*invr;\n    ax+=s*dx; ay+=s*dy; az+=s*dz;\n  }\n  Particle p=pi;\n  p.vx+=ax*dt; p.vy+=ay*dt; p.vz+=az*dt;\n  p.x+=p.vx*dt; p.y+=p.vy*dt; p.z+=p.vz*dt;\n  out[i]=p;\n}\nsrc/launch.json:\n{\"block\":256,\"items_per_block\":256,\"shared_memory_bytes\":0}\nThe controller must freshly check the full correctness suite and measure all three objective sizes; retain this candidate only if its results justify it.",
